## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a scalable, compliant telemetry pipeline with region isolation and real-time processing. It probes data modeling, idempotent semantics, and resilience at scale.

## Key Concepts
- Regional Pub/Sub and Dataflow streaming
- Schema validation and deduplication
- Tenant isolation via separate datasets and buckets
- Data residency and cross-region backups
- Observability and failover strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Dataflow transform sketch
function process(event) {
  if (!validateSchema(event)) throw new Error('Invalid');
  if (isDuplicate(event)) return;
  if (isAnomalous(event)) emit('anomaly', event);
  emitAggregates(event);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you allocate costs per tenant?
- How would you test end-to-end failover in a CI pipeline?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses real-time streaming design, multi-tenant isolation, data residency, and production-grade reliability in GCP.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub exact-once hints, Dataflow streaming, stateful processing
- Per-tenant IAM, separate buckets/service accounts, residency
- Hybrid scoring: rules engine + Vertex AI
- Dead-letter routing, canary deployments, observability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: streaming transform sketch
class ScoreDoFn {
  process(event) {
    const score = ruleScore(event) + mlScore(event);
    emit({ tenant: event.tenantId, id: event.id, score, ts: event.ts });
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate idempotence and exactly-once guarantees at scale?
- How would you test tenant isolation across regions and handle schema evolution?

## Why This Is Asked
